From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:45:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] x11: let the shell keep X11 windows on the X screen of
 a panned canvas

A shell that pans and zooms windows on a canvas larger than the monitors
moves X11 windows far outside the X screen. The X server keeps its
pointer on the screen, so clicks on those windows land at the screen's
edge, and window positions beyond 32767 do not fit in the protocol.

The shell can now move the X screen's origin among the windows. X11
windows get X positions relative to it: configuring windows and their
frames, configure requests and notifies, move and resize messages, size
hint positions, override-redirect windows and drag and drop positions
all go through it, and moving the origin moves every X11 window on the
X server and tells its client. Window menus requested in window
coordinates and move and resize requests from X11 clients also follow
the window group's transform.
